mats change without notice (fabrication is version-pinned, bootstrap\n175\tis the recovery path); transcript content can include secrets (the ledger\n176\tredacts at capture and sync time, but matching is pattern/entropy-based and\n177\tcannot catch every secret — review before sharing still matters); full\n178\thistories can exceed the target's context (size is reported before launch);\n179\tcrashes mid-turn leave partial capture, which the ledger tolerates by design.\n180\t\n181\t## Roadmap\n182\t\n183\tToward an npm release (decided 2026-07-21; deepen the two existing targets\n184\tbefore broadening):\n185\t\n186\t- Publish `conversation-ledger` to npm (name is unclaimed), then swap the\n187\t  `file:` dependency for a semver range — `prepublishOnly` refuses to publish\n188\t  until this happens. Deliberately deferred while both packages are iterated\n189\t  on and dogfooded for a few days.\n190\t- Adapter-drift automation stays **reporting-only** (decided 2026-08-02). The\n191\t  daily check (`.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml`) opens a tracking issue on\n192\t  drift and now closes it when drift clears; it never writes to the repo.\n193\t  Auto-drafting the revalidation PR was built and then reverted. The reasoning\n194\t  is worth keeping, because the idea is tempting enough to recur: CI cannot\n195\t  validate a pin — the probes need both target CLIs installed, a TTY for the\n196\t  interactive smoke test, and paid model credentials per provider to make the\n197\t  recall turns real. So any PR CI opened would be a mechanical one-line bump\n198\t  with nothing behind it, saving a trivial edit while creating a *mergeable*\n199\t  artifact that asserts a validation nobody performed. An issue cannot be\n200\t  merged, and that asymmetry is the point. The agent-drafted variant (the old\n201\t  stage 2, needing an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` secret) fails for the same reason —\n202\t  the API key was never the binding constraint; the provider credentials the\n203\t  prob